WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.850
AI agents should be tested before deployment and whenever their models, prompts, tools, data sources, permissions, or workflows change.

2
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:21.212
Testing can combine unit checks for policy code, integration tests for tool boundaries, scenario tests for complete workflows, and controlled evaluations of confusing or untrusted content.

3
00:00:21.212 --> 00:00:25.772
Testing should remain safe, authorized, and focused on defensive assurance.

4
00:00:25.772 --> 00:00:39.372
Important areas include instruction handling, permission enforcement, tool argument validation, data exposure, memory behavior, failure modes, approval workflows, logging, and safe shutdown.

5
00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.565
Tests should verify both allowed and denied behavior.

6
00:00:42.565 --> 00:00:52.792
A useful result is not merely that the agent produced a good answer, but that surrounding controls prevented an unauthorized action when model behavior was imperfect.

7
00:00:52.792 --> 00:00:56.035
Governance gives these controls ownership and continuity.

8
00:00:56.035 --> 00:01:11.999
Organizations should maintain an inventory of agents, accountable owners, intended use, risk tier, connected tools, data classes, model and prompt versions, approval requirements, monitoring expectations, and review dates.

9
00:01:11.999 --> 00:01:19.153
Changes that expand capability should trigger security and business review rather than quietly inheriting the original approval.

10
00:01:19.153 --> 00:01:22.216
Production evidence should drive continuous improvement.

11
00:01:22.216 --> 00:01:30.338
Teams can review incidents, near misses, blocked actions, user feedback, drift, access changes, and test results.

12
00:01:30.338 --> 00:01:36.743
Governance should help the organization make deliberate risk decisions without turning every update into paperwork.

13
00:01:36.743 --> 00:01:43.488
The goal is an agent capability that remains aligned with policy, business need, and risk tolerance over time.
